  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 803.03 Public Notice of the Availability of Unregulated Contaminant Monitoring Results",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 803.03 Public Notice of the Availability of Unregulated Contaminant Monitoring Results.\n\n(a) The O/O of a PWS at which monitoring under the unregulated contaminant monitoring rule identified in 40 CFR 141.40 is conducted shall issue public notice of the availability of the monitoring results to persons served by the PWS as specified in (b) through (e) below.\n\n(b) The notice shall contain the information specified in Env-Dw 801.03.\n\n(c) Within 12 months of the receipt of the results, the O/O of a CWS shall issue the notice either in accordance with Env-Dw 801.08(b) through (d) or through the CCR in accordance with Env-Dw 801.19.\n\n(d) Within 12 months of the receipt of the results, the O/O of an NTNCWS shall issue the notice in accordance with Env-Dw 801.11(b) and (c).\n\n(e) Within 10 days of providing notice to its customers, the O/O of a PWS shall submit the certification specified in Env-Dw 801.18 to the department.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 800) #9730, eff 6-30-10; ss by #12675, eff 1-1-19; ss by #14428, eff 11-21-25, EXPIRES 11-21-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw800.html"
